<article class="env-lemma" id="01O2">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/01O2">Lemma <span data-tag="01O2">27.16.9</span>.</a> Let $S$ be a scheme and $\mathcal{A}$ be a quasi-coherent sheaf of graded $\mathcal{O}_ S$-algebras. The morphism $\pi : \underline{\text{Proj}}_ S(\mathcal{A}) \to S$ is separated. </p>
</article> 
</p>
<article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      To prove a morphism is separated we may work locally on the base, see Schemes, Section <a href="/tag/01KH" data-tag="01KH">26.21</a>. By construction $\underline{\text{Proj}}_ S(\mathcal{A})$ is over any affine $U \subset S$ isomorphic to $\text{Proj}(A)$ with $A = \mathcal{A}(U)$. By Lemma <a href="/tag/01MC" data-tag="01MC">27.8.8</a> we see that $\text{Proj}(A)$ is separated. Hence $\text{Proj}(A) \to U$ is separated (see Schemes, Lemma <a href="/tag/01KV" data-tag="01KV">26.21.13</a>) as desired. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>
